# Modern Web Guidance

For HTML, CSS, and client-side JavaScript in `apps/web`, `apps/superadmin`, `apps/supplier`, and `packages/shared`, read and follow `.agents/skills/modern-web-guidance/SKILL.md` (linked at `.cursor/skills/modern-web-guidance`) before writing UI, layout, animation, forms, or browser API code. Search with `npx modern-web-guidance@latest search "<query>"`, then `retrieve` the matching guide.

Do not use this skill for `quanluong-app-be`, Docker, Python services, CI, or other backend and infra work.

This does not replace project skills that already govern the same files:

- `mobile-first` still owns narrow-screen layout (changes only at `max-width: 1023px`; desktop from `lg` stays pixel-stable).
- `impeccable` still owns design, craft, and visual direction when that skill applies.
- `unified-page-scroll` still owns page scroll owners and sticky layers.

Browser support stays Baseline Widely available unless the task states a different target. Do not enable origin trials or volatile features.
